      "- **Every read is fenced to the calling session's domain.** A session may read its own page, any page in its domain's `reach`, and — if the domain reaches the whole workspace — any page in that workspace. Anything else is **refused**, including a page whose domain cannot be determined at all: an unassigned page is not readable, it is a refusal. Every refusal writes a `read.refused` audit row naming the page and both domains. (Underneath that sits Notion's own share list, which the next paragraph is careful about.)",
